<!-- ── FOOTNOTES ── -->
<div class="footnote">
  <div class="fn-box">
    <div class="fn-title">Two HITL Gates — Human Always in Control</div>
    Gate 1 (Step 5): User decides whether to try the AI-suggested fix. Gate 2 (Step 7): User reviews and approves the L2 escalation template before any Jira ticket is created. At no point does the AI take a consequential action without explicit user confirmation.
  </div>
  <div class="fn-box">
    <div class="fn-title">Manual Rerun — By Design</div>
    The end user manually applies the L1 fix and re-runs the Genie Bot batch file on their own machine. The AI provides the instructions; the human executes. This eliminates any risk of automated code execution on user machines and is the correct governance posture for a CIB environment.
  </div>
  <div class="fn-box">
    <div class="fn-title">L1 Attempt Always Recorded</div>
    When a user tries the fix but it fails (Path B), the L2 escalation template automatically includes: what fix was suggested, that the user attempted it, and that it did not resolve the issue. L2 never needs to re-diagnose from scratch — full context is pre-populated in the ticket.
  </div>
</div>

